r policies cost no coin. They do not buy land, build improvements or cultivate biomes."],["LABEL",{},"Worker priority",["SELECT",{},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"balanced"},"Balanced"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"food"},"Food"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"industry"},"Industry"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"coin"},"Coin"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"knowledge"},"Knowledge"]]],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Food, Industry, Coin and Knowledge favor the highest yield of that type. Balanced favors food when reserves are low and also values industry, coin and knowledge. A focused policy can reduce other yields or leave a resource deposit unworked."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","class":"primary wide"},"Apply worker policy"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Returning to manual control keeps current assignments. Assigning or removing a worker yourself also ends the policy. Siege and occupation pause its assignments; losing the hearth ends it."]],["DETAILS",{"class":"land-policy","data-testid":"land-policy"},["SUMMARY",{},"Land commission",["SPAN",{},"Direct construction"]],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Build one chosen improvement on suitable worked tiles as this hearth develops. Applying a commission can pay for its first order immediately. Further orders begin after each turn’s upkeep and production charters."],["LABEL",{},"Commission improvement",["SELECT",{},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"improvement.terraced_fields"},"Terraced fields"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.managed_woodlot"},"Managed woodlot"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.quarry"},"Measured quarry"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.reedworks"},"Reedworks"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"improvement.shore_fishery"},"Shore fishery"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_se