ve the chosen treasury reserve. Other realm orders can still spend that reserve. Commissions share the treasury in stable hearth order."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Only unimproved, worked land is considered. A resource deposit accepts only its matching extraction site. Existing sites are kept; commissions do not claim land, cultivate biomes or assign workers."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Siege and occupation pause work. Ending a commission keeps paid work underway. Building, cultivating or cancelling land work yourself ends the commission after a successful order. Losing the hearth ends it; cancelled work is not refunded."]],["DETAILS",{"class":"land-options","data-testid":"settlement-road"},["SUMMARY",{},"Road connections"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Settlements gradually connect to an older town along a charted land route. Workers survey one town per realm each turn. Completed roads cross forest and hills for 1 movement point and remain after conquest."],["P",{},"Explore toward another owned settlement to establish a connection. Water and mountains require another route."]],["P",{"class":"land-stage","data-testid":"settlement-stage"},"colony"," · Capital"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Colony: 1–2 people · Settlement: 3–7 · City: 8+. Capital is a separate designation."],["P",{"data-testid":"land-counts"},"7"," claimed tiles · ","0"," / ","1"," assigned workers · reach ","2"],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Connected territory and population can keep growing. Each person can work one additional tile. Larger hearths need more food, investment and civic upkeep."],["P",{"class":"field-help","data-testid":"hearth-growth-economy"},"Next person: ","0"," / ","12"," food · consumption ","2"," food per turn · civic upkeep ","1"," coin (","1"," population, ","0"," territory, ","0"," administration)."],["P",{"class":"field-help"},"Realm coin per turn: ","7"," income − ","2"," upkeep = ","5",". Queued formations add ","0"," upkeep when completed."],["SECTION",{"class":"bord